{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"The process ownership design is largely consistent with D1: the CLI runs a separate shim as subreaper, and its adopted-child scan is confined to that shim’s subtree. I found two edge paths worth resolving before the verdict: a Linux CLI dispatch silently drops to the weaker environment scan if it cannot create the shim/pipe, and the shim currently includes PIDs in its “ended” list even when pidfd open or signaling reports `ESRCH`. I’m checking whether tests or subsequent run handling change either conclusion."}}
